  why: (S) => ({ h: 'Why current tax alone misleads', what: 'Lim earns the same profit every year, so the tax expense should be the same every year. With current tax only, it is not: years 1–3 are low and year 4 jumps, because tax law used up the machine’s deductions faster than the books.\nThe books use up the machine’s $120,000 at $30,000 a year; tax law at $40,000 a year. After year 1, tax law has already used $10,000 more of the deductions than the books, so a later year will have $10,000 less to deduct, and its taxable profit will be higher. That extra tax is caused by year 1, so it belongs in year 1: deferred tax records it now.\n**Objective:** account for the current and future tax effects of a transaction in the same period, and in the same place (P&L, OCI or equity), as the transaction.',
